  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I still think the best solution is a yellow status option that shows where you are but still needs to request if you want to go in unless someone else of your friends is in the same instance as green/blue\n\nAn existence of a yellow status will move a lot of people out of orange though. More options is just better for everyone\n\nWhy add them on your friends list if you want to avoid them that hard? Yellow status is still best. Yellow gang yellow gang we'll make it happen one day\n\nIf it's convenient for you to see others that are green then won't it be nice to reciprocate to also show yourself in green? It's only fair and is an equivalent exchange of energies. As of right now orange has the upper ground always, there is no balancing fairness in the dynamic\n\nYellow solves the issue of you don’t want to handle someone right now since they can only join you if they have another friend there they’ll be joining on instead\n\nYellow is mainly for visibility so everyone knows something is happening somewhere\n\nBenefits friends+ worlds most\n\nOrange can exist but only if Yellow is a thing too.\n\nThe number one reason people say they go into orange status is:\n\n\"So people I know who won't mesh with the current social environment won't join\"\n\nIf there is another person there that they can join on then it's fine isn't it since they obviously can and your filtering does not need to occur while benefiting everyone else to broadcast what you are currently potentially doing.\n\nWhich goes to the next point of if people know what map you are in they can have a better guess if they would want to request join on you. Instead of them requesting join on you then seeing it's for an activity they didn't want to join anyways and it'll all just be a waste of a join request. And if there is anyone there in the map who is a friend of them anyways then they can just immediately join.\n\nThis aims to solve the issue of needing to send 25+ invite requests to orange people to even get one accept invite.\n\nAnd the awkwardness that occurs when a friend of yours didn't accept your request invite but when you joined another friend of yours, the person who rejected your invite request is there... now with yellow status you could just join no issues as long as you have another friend there.",
